Task 1: Configure Backup Strategies Using ipa-backup
Subtask 1.1: Understanding IdM Backup Types
Before implementing backup strategies, it's important to understand the different types of backups available in IdM:

Full Backup: Contains all IdM data including:

LDAP database
Certificate Authority (CA) data
Configuration files
Logs and metadata
Data-only Backup: Contains only the LDAP data without logs or temporary files

Subtask 1.2: Prepare the Backup Environment
First, let's prepare the system for backup operations:

# Switch to root user
sudo su -

# Create a dedicated backup directory
mkdir -p /var/lib/ipa/backup/manual
chmod 700 /var/lib/ipa/backup/manual

# Check available disk space
df -h /var/lib/ipa/backup/

# Verify IdM server status
ipactl status
Subtask 1.3: Perform a Full System Backup
Execute a comprehensive full backup of the IdM server:

# Create a full backup with timestamp
ipa-backup --verbose --data --logs

# Alternative: Create backup with custom location
ipa-backup --verbose --data --logs --dir=/var/lib/ipa/backup/manual

# Check the backup creation
ls -la /var/lib/ipa/backup/
The backup process will create a directory with timestamp containing all necessary files.

Subtask 1.4: Create Data-Only Backup
For faster backup operations, create a data-only backup:

# Create data-only backup
ipa-backup --data --verbose

# Verify backup contents
BACKUP_DIR=$(ls -t /var/lib/ipa/backup/ | head -1)
ls -la /var/lib/ipa/backup/$BACKUP_DIR/
Subtask 1.5: Implement Automated Backup Script
Create an automated backup script for regular backup operations:

# Create backup script
cat > /usr/local/bin/idm-backup.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

# IdM Automated Backup Script
BACKUP_BASE="/var/lib/ipa/backup"
LOG_FILE="/var/log/idm-backup.log"
RETENTION_DAYS=30

# Function to log messages
log_message() {
    echo "$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') - $1" >> $LOG_FILE
}

# Start backup process
log_message "Starting IdM backup process"

# Check if IdM is running
if ! ipactl status > /dev/null 2>&1; then
    log_message "ERROR: IdM services are not running"
    exit 1
fi

# Perform backup
if ipa-backup --data --logs --verbose >> $LOG_FILE 2>&1; then
    log_message "Backup completed successfully"
else
    log_message "ERROR: Backup failed"
    exit 1
fi

# Clean old backups
find $BACKUP_BASE -type d -name "ipa-full-*" -mtime +$RETENTION_DAYS -exec rm -rf {} \; 2>/dev/null

log_message "Backup process completed"
EOF

# Make script executable
chmod +x /usr/local/bin/idm-backup.sh

# Test the script
/usr/local/bin/idm-backup.sh
Subtask 1.6: Schedule Regular Backups
Set up automated backups using cron:

# Create cron job for daily backups
cat > /etc/cron.d/idm-backup << 'EOF'
# IdM Daily Backup
0 2 * * * root /usr/local/bin/idm-backup.sh
EOF

# Verify cron job
crontab -l
cat /etc/cron.d/idm-backup
Task 2: Restore IdM Server from Backup
Subtask 2.1: Prepare for Restore Operation
Before restoring, ensure the system is properly prepared:

# Stop all IdM services
ipactl stop

# Verify all services are stopped
ipactl status

# Create a pre-restore backup (safety measure)
cp -r /var/lib/ipa /var/lib/ipa.pre-restore.$(date +%Y%m%d)
Subtask 2.2: Identify Available Backups
List and examine available backup files:

# List all available backups
ls -la /var/lib/ipa/backup/

# Get detailed information about the latest backup
LATEST_BACKUP=$(ls -t /var/lib/ipa/backup/ | head -1)
echo "Latest backup: $LATEST_BACKUP"

# Examine backup contents
ls -la /var/lib/ipa/backup/$LATEST_BACKUP/
Subtask 2.3: Perform Full Restore Operation
Execute the restore process using the most recent backup:

# Restore from the latest backup
ipa-restore --verbose /var/lib/ipa/backup/$LATEST_BACKUP

# Alternative: Restore with specific options
# ipa-restore --data --logs --verbose /var/lib/ipa/backup/$LATEST_BACKUP
Subtask 2.4: Verify Restore Success
After restoration, verify that all components are working correctly:

# Start IdM services
ipactl start

# Check service status
ipactl status

# Verify LDAP connectivity
ldapsearch -x -b "dc=example,dc=com" -s base

# Test IdM functionality
ipa user-find admin
ipa host-find
Subtask 2.5: Handle Restore Issues
If the restore encounters problems, follow these troubleshooting steps:

# Check IdM logs for errors
tail -f /var/log/ipaserver-install.log

# Verify directory server logs
tail -f /var/log/dirsrv/slapd-EXAMPLE-COM/errors

# Check certificate status
ipa-cacert-manage list

# Restart services if needed
ipactl restart
Task 3: Test Disaster Recovery Procedures
Subtask 3.1: Create Test Scenario
Simulate a disaster scenario to test recovery procedures:

# Create test users and groups before disaster simulation
ipa user-add testuser1 --first=Test --last=User1 --password
ipa user-add testuser2 --first=Test --last=User2 --password
ipa group-add testgroup --desc="Test group for DR testing"
ipa group-add-member testgroup --users=testuser1,testuser2

# Verify test objects exist
ipa user-find testuser
ipa group-show testgroup
Subtask 3.2: Simulate System Failure
Create a controlled failure scenario:

# Create a backup before simulation
ipa-backup --data --logs --verbose

# Stop IdM services
ipactl stop

# Simulate data corruption (CAUTION: Only in test environment)
mv /var/lib/dirsrv /var/lib/dirsrv.corrupted
mv /var/lib/ipa /var/lib/ipa.corrupted

# Attempt to start services (should fail)
ipactl start
ipactl status
Subtask 3.3: Execute Recovery Procedures
Follow the complete disaster recovery process:

# Step 1: Restore directory structure
mkdir -p /var/lib/dirsrv
mkdir -p /var/lib/ipa

# Step 2: Find the backup to restore
RECOVERY_BACKUP=$(ls -t /var/lib/ipa/backup/ | head -1)
echo "Using backup: $RECOVERY_BACKUP"

# Step 3: Perform restoration
ipa-restore --verbose /var/lib/ipa/backup/$RECOVERY_BACKUP

# Step 4: Start services
ipactl start

# Step 5: Verify service status
ipactl status
Subtask 3.4: Validate Recovery Success
Thoroughly test all IdM functionality after recovery:

# Test authentication
kinit admin

# Verify test users still exist
ipa user-find testuser
ipa group-show testgroup

# Test LDAP operations
ldapsearch -x -b "dc=example,dc=com" "(uid=testuser1)"

# Verify DNS functionality
dig @localhost example.com

# Test certificate operations
ipa cert-find

# Check replication status (if applicable)
ipa-replica-manage list
