## Troubleshooting Common Issues

### Backup Issues

**Problem**: Backup fails with permission errors
```bash
# Solution: Check and fix permissions
chown -R dirsrv:dirsrv /var/lib/dirsrv
chmod -R 755 /var/lib/ipa/backup
Problem: Insufficient disk space for backup

# Solution: Clean old backups and check space
df -h /var/lib/ipa/backup/
find /var/lib/ipa/backup -name "ipa-full-*" -mtime +7 -exec rm -rf {} \;
Restore Issues
Problem: Restore fails with database errors

# Solution: Stop services and retry
ipactl stop
systemctl stop dirsrv@EXAMPLE-COM
ipa-restore --verbose [BACKUP_PATH]
Problem: Services won't start after restore

# Solution: Check logs and restart individual services
tail -f /var/log/ipaserver-install.log
systemctl restart dirsrv@EXAMPLE-COM
systemctl restart krb5kdc
systemctl restart kadmin
Best Practices
Regular Testing: Test restore procedures monthly
Multiple Backup Locations: Store backups on separate storage systems
Documentation: Keep recovery procedures updated and accessible
Monitoring: Implement backup success/failure monitoring
Retention Policy: Maintain appropriate backup retention periods
Security: Encrypt backup files and secure storage locations
